{
  "abstract": "There are infinitely many primes p for which p - 2 has an odd number of prime factors, counted with multiplicity. A second theorem gives such a prime above every natural bound and explicitly records p - 2 > 0. Both statements have no additional hypotheses. The standalone Lean development includes its supporting analytic number theory and uses Mathlib as its only direct Lake dependency.",
